& [VerbatimUserMessage] is the preserved user message
  + [text] is "so I'm thinking of this along the lines as what we're doing is creating a language model from Cantor, because essentially that's what it means to have a path of semantic coherence that directs the model to reflect on the prescribed pattern as the prompt stimulates. I'm just wondering how far to take it, because we could fold it into an execution layer with llama.cpp. I'm planning on experimenting with a \"shared inference\" forward pass where llama.cpp has a tool interface customized for a virtual pipeline between inference here and inference there, pipe it in to llama.cpp to join a LLM."

